    "name": {
      "value": "The Fool"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "sf3"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "_The Fool_ represents grave foolishness, grand naivete, and exceptional greed. As long as you have _The Fool_ invested, anytime you gain the stupefied condition, reduce its value by 1. You also gain a +2 item bonus to all saving throws against effects that cause the stupefied condition. This bonus increases to +3 if you're at least 17th level.\n\n- **Activate:** 2 Actions\n- **Traits:** mental\n- **Frequency:** once per day\n\nYou display _The Fool_ to your foes in a clumsy, awkward, and embarrassing way. Choose up to four creatures within 60 feet. These four creatures must attempt a Will save against your class DC.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The creature is unaffected.\n- **Success:** The creature is distracted by your antics and is stupefied 1 until the start of your next turn.\n- **Failure:** The creature is stupefied 2.\n- **Critical Failure:** The creature is stupefied 3. In addition, for 1 minute, the creature is confused."
    },
